      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَنَّ</span></b> : see R. Q. 1, in four places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَنِنَ</span> is
mentioned by Golius and Freytag (by the
former as from the S) as though it were the verb
of which <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَنَنٌ</span> (q. v.) is the inf. n.; but I find no
authority for it: and if <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَنَنٌ</span> have a verb, it
should, accord. to rule, be <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَنَّ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَدَنُّ</span>.]

